{"author":{"id":"698145999e8f05e141e1b3e41afea48de9004817a883a692985b3265ceb5f427"},"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"698145999e8f05e141e1b3e41afea48de9004817a883a692985b3265ceb5f427"},"timestamp":1788986426,"metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDODbKJfs8AAAABQiJIGA","github-url":"https://github.com/vmiklos/plees-tracker/issues/601","origin":"github"},"nonce":"fHEfndvQ7q2CQBzX7YR8tU9WKz0=","title":"help seeing Start/Stop buttons at night half-awake","message":"The problem: the Start/Stop button is floating above other text, which makes it extremely hard to find it on the screen, and read the label at night, half-awake in the bed. So you have to try to focus on it more, which will wake your brain up a bit, and makes it harder to fall asleep again.\n\nIt would be awesome, if the floating buttons would become\n* positioned inside the scrollable area at a fixed location\n* get a large (huge) area, so you would not need to get so specific in your motoric skills to tap it\n* this is important: get huge, double line emojis before the text, like: \n```\n🛏️ Start        🐓 Woke\n   sleep            up\n```\n\nMy personnal recommendation is the line below the Dashboard, and above the \"Past sleeps\", because the easiest place to tap a mobile phone screen is in the middle. If you want to tap at the top, your thumb needs to stretch, and your hand holding the phone below needs to change a bit. If there buttons are at the bottom, the phone becomes top-heavy, and your holding hand needs to change position again.\n\nAlso, i think, the \"Status\" line could go right next to these buttons.","files":null}]}